{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Implement batching for the Rabbit sink using Spring AMQP's native batching capabilities.",
    "Configure Gradle build scripts to declare Spring XD dependencies as 'provided' and apply the Boot plugin with 'MODULE' layout.",
    "Design compression support to be extensible via standard Spring configuration, allowing users to inject custom compression codecs.",
    "Make the database requirement conditional using Spring profiles or environment properties to support DIRT runtime without a DB.",
    "Define a clear core interface contract for RxJava processor modules to ensure seamless integration with the Spring XD module ecosystem."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The developer has prior experience with Spring XD, Spring Boot, and Gradle.",
    "A workaround for the Spring Boot module layout scoping issue (#2187) can be implemented without modifying Spring Boot core.",
    "Existing performance benchmarking infrastructure is available and can be easily configured for new test scenarios.",
    "The DIRT runtime can be modified or configured to skip database initialization when stream processing is the only requirement.",
    "Acceptance testing frameworks for the hdfs-dataset module are already established, requiring only the addition of specific test cases."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Implement Rabbit Sink Batching",
      "activity_description": "Add the option of batching for the Rabbit sink so that data can be written in batches instead of one-at-a-time (U1).",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "Implement Gradle Build Option for Module Projects",
      "activity_description": "Create a Gradle build option to support module projects declaring Spring XD dependencies as provided, configuring the boot plugin for 'MODULE' layout, and handling boilerplate build configuration (U2).",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "Add Acceptance Test Coverage for HDFS-Dataset Module",
      "activity_description": "Include acceptance test coverage for the hdfs-dataset module to validate functionality as part of every CI build (U3).",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "Extend Compression Support",
      "activity_description": "Add an option to extend compression support so that users can override the defaults and customize as needed (U4).",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "Performance Testing - Batching on Rabbit",
      "activity_description": "Rerun baseline benchmarks with batching enabled on Rabbit to compare results with previous performance snapshots (U5).",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "Performance Testing - Compression on Rabbit",
      "activity_description": "Rerun baseline benchmarks with compression enabled on Rabbit to compare results with previous performance snapshots (U6).",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "Implement Option to Disable DB Requirement",
      "activity_description": "Add an option to disable the DB requirement so that users can setup to use DIRT runtime when stream processing is the only requirement (U7).",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "Implement Core Interface Contract for RxJava Processor",
      "activity_description": "Implement the core interface contract so that users can create a processor module that uses the RxJava API (U8).",
      "most_likely_effort": 5
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 25
  }
}
```

